; Sprites: hatted walker, left and right (8 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $B400+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. A figure in a hat and robe with an outstretched arm, walking. Frames
; 0-3 are used while moving left, 4-7 while moving right (bit 7 of entity byte +0). Used by entity definitions $40 $41
; $42 $43 $4A $4B $4C $4D $4E $4F $50 $51 $67 in rooms $13 $1B $1C $1F $31 (eight of them in The Forgotten Abbey, room
; $13).
@label=SpritesHatWalkers
